# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mokosh Client - environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit. Values are read by `docker compose`
# and forwarded into the dev container, where `dx serve` invokes `cargo` /
# `rustc` and bakes them into the WASM bundle via `option_env!`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Login bypass (DEV ONLY).
#
# When both ADMIN_EMAIL and ADMIN_PASSWORD are set AND non-empty at compile
# time, the WASM client starts pre-authenticated as this admin user and the
# login screen redirects straight to the dashboard. Bypass is baked into the
# bundle at build time; changing these values requires rebuilding.
#
# Leave both unset (or empty) to use the normal login screen.
#
# Do NOT use these values outside local development. The bundle is shipped
# to every browser - anyone who downloads it can read both fields.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=devpassword12

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-portal host (build-time fallback).
#
# MAPPS-649 replaced the pre-649 per-MSP subdomain shape
# (MOKOSH_PORTAL_HOST_SUFFIX, which needed a DNS wildcard and a matching
# TLS SAN) with a single portal host every deploy serves the portal
# from. `oci-build/entrypoint.sh` writes this into `_mokosh_config.js`
# from MOKOSH_PORTAL_HOST on the mokosh-apps container so a rebuild is
# not needed to change it in prod. In dev (dx serves the assets
# directly without an entrypoint) the SPA reads this env var via
# `option_env!()` as a compile-time fallback.
#
# Value is a bare host (no scheme, no leading dot), typically
# `portal.<apex>`. The SPA uses it to build the "portal login URL" the
# tenant-create modal previews and the "Copy portal link" affordance
# offers; the portal itself is served by the server and works whether
# or not this is set (unset leaves the SPA showing a generic hint
# instead of a broken URL).
#
# In dev leave empty; there is no `.client.localhost` shape any more.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOKOSH_PORTAL_HOST=portal.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OIDC client ID for `just dev-sso` (compose.dev-sso.yml) ONLY.
#
# Run `just register-dev-clients` in the bunyip repo to upsert an SPA client
# into bunyip-api, then set this to the resulting client_id (a UUID). Not
# needed unless you run `just dev-sso`; leaving it unset fails loud there
# instead of silently using a wrong client_id.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOKOSH_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
